-- CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED policy — coverage logic.
--
-- Isomorphic to the source contract: §1 (policy in effect), §2 (benefits),
-- §3 (general exclusions), §4.2 (arbitration precondition to liability).
-- §4.1/4.3/4.4/4.5 are payment/jurisdiction/mechanics clauses, not coverage
-- gates, and are not separately encoded as boolean conditions.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Fact schema (verbatim from bench/schema-l4.md)`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                          IS A NUMBER
      `confined in us hospital`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuous confinement days`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `claim made setting out basis`                IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Supporting helpers (verbatim from bench/schema-l4.md — do not redefine)`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `§1 — Policy in effect`

§§ `§1.3 — wellness visit and written confirmation`

-- §1.3: confirmation of the wellness visit must be supplied no later than
-- the 7th month anniversary, of a visit (with a qualified provider) that
-- itself occurred no later than the 6th month anniversary.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness confirmation given timely` claim MEANS
       `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
   AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
   AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`

-- §1.1(3): the §1.3 condition keeps the policy in effect either because it
-- has already been satisfied on time, or because — at the time of THIS
-- hospitalization — its 7-month deadline has not yet arrived, so it is
-- "still pending" rather than failed.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness confirmation timely or pending` claim MEANS
  `wellness confirmation given timely` claim OR claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7

§§ `§1.2 — cancellation`

-- §1.2's other cancellation triggers: fraud, misrepresentation, or the
-- policy having run past its one-year term. (Failure to satisfy §1.3 on
-- time is already the negation of the helper above, so it is not repeated
-- here.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cancellation triggered` claim MEANS
       isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
    OR isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
    OR claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

§§ `§1.1 — the four conditions for being in effect`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect` claim MEANS
        claim's `agreement signed`
    AND isJust (claim's `premium paid month`)
    AND `wellness confirmation timely or pending` claim
    AND NOT `cancellation triggered` claim

§ `§2 — Benefits`

-- §2.1: the hospitalization must be a result of sickness or accidental
-- injury — not, e.g., a deliberate, non-accidental act.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization ground covered` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither             THEN FALSE

-- §2.2: the daily benefit only runs for continuous confinement, capped at
-- 365 days. An unrecorded/ongoing day-count does not itself breach the cap.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`confinement within benefit period` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `continuous confinement days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d AT MOST 365

-- §2.1/§2.2/§2.3 together: confined (in a US hospital, per §2.2's literal
-- text) for a covered ground, within the day cap, with a claim made
-- setting out the basis for it.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospital benefit payable` claim MEANS
        `hospitalization ground covered` claim
    AND claim's `confined in us hospital`
    AND `confinement within benefit period` claim
    AND claim's `claim made setting out basis`

§ `§3 — General exclusions`

-- §3.1: excluded if the sickness/injury arose out of skydiving, military
-- service, firefighting, or police service — or if the claimant was 80 or
-- older at the time of hospitalization. Note this is about what the
-- sickness/injury actually arose out of, not the claimant's occupation.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded` claim MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
    OR claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§ `§4.2 — Arbitration, as a condition precedent to liability`

-- §4.2.1: once parties are unable to settle, arbitration must be commenced
-- within 3 months of that point.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced timely` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (m PLUS 3)

-- §4.2.1: a valid arbitration award is a condition precedent to liability,
-- on top of timely commencement.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration resolved` claim MEANS
       `arbitration commenced timely` claim
   AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`

-- The arbitration machinery only bites once a dispute has actually arisen.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration precondition met` claim MEANS
  NOT (claim's `dispute arisen`) OR `arbitration resolved` claim

-- §4.2.1: recovery may not be sought until 60 days after written proof of
-- claim was submitted. The schema's clocks are all in months, so the
-- 60-day wait is approximated as 2 months; this never binds unless
-- recovery has actually been sought.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery wait respected` claim MEANS
  CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
      CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST p  THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

§ `covered`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
        `policy in effect` claim
    AND `hospital benefit payable` claim
    AND NOT `excluded` claim
    AND `arbitration precondition met` claim
    AND `recovery wait respected` claim
